Hi,

I am running a mantel test on my dataset. As my species is a marine species, I calculated a distance matrix by the closest distance following the coastline and then converted the matrix into synthetic coordinates with the command:

DistMat<-viamaris(loccoor,extent.buffer = 5)

syncoor<-isoMDS(DistMat)

But when I tried to run the ibd:

ibd<-gl.ibd(x, distance = syncoor)

it comes up an error:

Analysis performed on the genlight object.

Error in .pointsToMatrix(p) : longitude < -720

It seems like that the error is because some of my longitude value is <-720. I did have some value <-720 after converting into synthetic coordinates. I am not sure it is normal that I can't run the command with this condition.

