Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/dartr/c/YgtkO7T0VZM/m/LUlSURDxAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Zoriana,

Not sure if I understand your create synthetic coordintes approach using the MDS.

So you have a data.frame (assuming) that has two columns. Name those two columns ( “x” and “y”) and then you can

Run

colnames(syncoor) <- c(“x”,”y”)

gl.ibd(x, coordinates=syncoor)

This calculates Fst and again “Euclidean” distances  based on the coordinates.

That should work.

But you could also provide Dgen and Dgeo to  gl.ibd (providing the matrices) directly and then you do not need your mds (which looses some of the distance information as you convert it to a two dimensional distance [how much you loose depends on you stress value]).

Hope that helps,

Bernd

p.s. Is there a paper that describes your approach?

Finally there is a least-cost implementation also in dartR if that helps…. gl.genleastcost

